 {
  "id": "2105353453815861370",
  "url": "https://x.com/warpdotdev/status/2105353453815861370",
  "author_username": "warpdotdev",
  "author_name": "Warp",
  "created_at": "2026-09-30T17:45:53.000Z",
  "text": "Agents are getting complex to manage: models, skills, automations, permissions, cloud environments, orchestration patterns...\n\nSo, we built the Terraform for agents: one repository that configures all of your agents as code.\n\nThe Warp Factories configuration spec defines:\n- Agents and orchestration: how work gets routed and which models agents use\n- Automations: the events and schedules that kick off work\n- Access and environments: repositories, secrets, MCP servers, and runners\n- Measurement: scorers and benchmarks for understanding and improving performance\n\nBecause it’s all code, both engineers and agents can propose changes to the factory itself. That makes it possible to test new configurations, benchmark them, and even have your factory propose improvements as PRs.",
  "public_metrics": {
   "bookmark_count": 79,
   "impression_count": 955198,
